FILE LibKa0s/OptionsKeybinds.lua: KEYBINDS_MINOR 1 -> 2 (`Minor 2:` note). `lib.__AttachKeybinds(O, d)` defines:
1. `O.KEYBINDS_UNCHANGED = lib.KEYBIND_STRINGS.UNCHANGED`, the sentence a host appends to its General page's `opts.defaultsTooltip` (Options.lua:647, drawn at :786).
2. `O.KeybindingsTab(spec)` -> a host-tab entry for `O.RenderTabbedSchema`'s `opts.tabs` (docblock OptionsTabs.lua:1294-1297: `{ key, label, tooltip, before, render = function(ctx, rows) }`, run by renderHostTab :1241-1250 under pcall with `ctx.__renderDisabled` set): `{ key = spec.key or "Keybindings", label = S.TAB_LABEL, tooltip = S.TAB_TIP, before = spec.before, render = function(ctx) O.KeybindRows(ctx, spec) end }` where S = lib.KEYBIND_STRINGS merged with spec.strings. spec: `bindings` (array of `{ command, tooltip }`, row order; the host's NS.BINDINGS), `key`, `before` (nil = last), `intro` (optional ONE extra host line drawn under the fixed INTRO; it never replaces it), `strings` (translations of lib.KEYBIND_STRINGS keys). A hand-drawn strip (LootHistory's GENERAL_TABS, settings/Panel.lua:972-980, selected at :1022-1023) adds `{ key = "Keybindings", build = function(ctx) O.KeybindRows(ctx, SPEC) end }`.
3. `O.KeybindRows(ctx, spec, parent)` -> array of row records `{ command, label, group, slots = { w1, w2 }, clear, status }` (for tests) or nil when degraded. parent defaults to `O.EnsureScroll(ctx)` (Options.lua:853); with no AceGUI or scroll return nil having drawn nothing.
   - Degradation: `not lib.__keybindAvailable()` -> one `O.TextRow(ctx, S.UNAVAILABLE)` (OptionsWidgets.lua:583), return nil.
   - Intro: `O.TextRow(ctx, S.INTRO)` always; then `spec.intro` as a second TextRow when it is a non-empty string; then `O.AddSpacer(scroll, O.ROW_VSPACER)` (OptionsWidgets.lua:541, Options.lua:525).
   - One row per binding: AceGUI SimpleGroup (Flow, full width) with a Label of `GetBindingName(command)` (fallback `_G["BINDING_NAME_"..command]` or the command; no label is passed in) at relative width 0.40; Key 1 and Key 2 AceGUI Buttons (0.22 each) showing `GetBindingText(key)` (fallback the key) or NOT_BOUND; a Clear Button (0.12). Widths sum below 1 (options-ui-§8 clip inset). Tooltips via `O.AttachTooltip(widget, label, tooltip)` (OptionsWidgets.lua:512): the row's spec tooltip on the label, S.SLOT_TIP on slots, S.CLEAR_TIP on Clear. A binding whose command is not a string is skipped and printed with `lib.STRINGS.ROW_FAILED` (Options.lua:220).
   - Under the rows two Labels: the set line `(S.SET_ACCOUNT or S.SET_CHARACTER, from lib.__keybindSetName) .. " " .. S.SET_HOW`, and the status line (empty until an action).
   - `ctx.__renderDisabled`: slots and Clear SetDisabled(true).
   - Each row pushes a refresher into `ctx.refreshers` (Options.lua:713) that repaints its slots and the set line from GetBindingKey (no key cached).
   - Slot clicks: the slot's frame `RegisterForClicks("LeftButtonUp", "RightButtonUp")`, restored to "LeftButtonUp" in the widget's `OnRelease` callback so a pooled Button leaves with nothing of ours (options-ui-§19). OnClick callback (widget, event, button): RightButton -> refused through `O.__combatRefused("keybind", command)` (Options.lua:565) else `lib.__keybindClear(command, slot)`, status S.CLEARED; LeftButton -> start capture. Clear -> refused in combat, else `lib.__keybindClear(command, nil)`.
   - Capture: ONE library-level `lib.__keybindListener` (created once, kept across a LibStub upgrade like lib.__parkFrame, OptionsRegistry.lua:63-84; a plain Frame that draws nothing, frame-layering T0, no strata or level of its own). Start (refused through `O.__combatRefused` in combat, status S.COMBAT): stop any other capture; SetParent the listener to the slot's frame, SetAllPoints, `EnableKeyboard(true)`, `EnableMouse(true)`, `EnableMouseWheel(true)`, Show; slot text S.LISTENING. OnKeyDown(key): ESCAPE cancels (the keyboard-enabled frame consumes it, so the Settings window stays open; never SetPropagateKeyboardInput); PRINTSCREEN calls Screenshot() if present and keeps listening; else `chord = lib.__keyChord(key)`; nil keeps listening; else write. OnMouseDown(button): LeftButton or RightButton cancel (click again to cancel); others convert through __keyChord and write. OnMouseWheel(delta): MOUSEWHEELUP / MOUSEWHEELDOWN through __keyChord and write. Write = `lib.__keybindSet(command, slot, chord)`; status: ok and displacedUnbound -> KEY_UNBOUND_ERROR:format(GetBindingName(displaced)); ok -> KEY_BOUND; "combat" -> S.COMBAT; "failed" -> S.FAILED; then stop and repaint every row of this ctx. Stop: EnableKeyboard(false), EnableMouse(false), EnableMouseWheel(false), Hide, ClearAllPoints, SetParent(UIParent), restore the slot text from GetBindingKey. One listening row across every host.
   - Capture stops on: the slot widget's OnRelease (ClearScroll on a tab change or structural refresh, Options.lua:887); the page's OnHide (hook `ctx.panel` once per ctx, guarded by `ctx.__keybindHooked`); combat start: a library-level hook `lib.__keybindOnCombat` held strongly on lib and registered in `lib.__combatHooks` (Options.lua:362, weak-keyed; called by OptionsCombat.lua:117 as pcall(hook, locked)), replacing an older copy's hook on upgrade (`lib.__combatHooks[old] = nil`); on `locked == true` it stops any capture and writes S.COMBAT to that row's status. No new event registration for combat.
   - Every function CCN <= 15; the file stays < 1000 lines (if it would pass ~900, peel the capture listener into a secondary file paired on the shell's minor, per CLAUDE.md 'A peel here is a release').

