Design: KEYBINDINGS_RESEARCH.md §3.1 (UPDATE_BINDINGS keeps Blizzard's rows in sync; SetBinding very likely fires it as SaveBindings does; override bindings fire it too, so debounce), §3.4 (LoadBindings on a set switch fires it), §5.1 'Syncing' (one library registration only while a row is on screen, the lib.__syncCombatEvents discipline, OptionsCombat.lua:82-101; debounce; OnShow re-read). Risks 5 and 9 of §5.6.

REGISTRATION ROUTE: CLAUDE.md's `events-frames-taint-§1` register row (:77) lists three raw private registration sites and re-checks when 'a fourth private registration site appears in LibKa0s/'. Register through `core.SafeRegisterEvent(frame, "UPDATE_BINDINGS")` (Core.lua:481, pcall'd; a Frame ignores the handler argument), so this is not a fourth raw site. OptionsKeybinds.lua takes `local core = LibStub and LibStub("LibKa0s-Core-1.0", true)`. Unregister with the frame's UnregisterEvent. Without core.SafeRegisterEvent register nothing; the OnShow re-read and refreshers still work. Add one sentence to that row's Why cell: OptionsKeybinds registers through SafeRegisterEvent on purpose.

FILE LibKa0s/OptionsKeybinds.lua: KEYBINDS_MINOR 2 -> 3 (`Minor 3:` note).
- `lib.__keybindLive`: weak-keyed set row-record -> ctx, added when a row is built, removed in the row group's OnRelease.
- `lib.__keybindEventFrame`: one hidden Frame created once, kept across upgrades; its OnEvent looks `lib.__OnKeybindEvent` up at call time (the OptionsCombat.lua:138-148 idiom).
- `lib.__syncKeybindEvents()`: drop dead rows; a row is on screen when its group frame answers IsVisible() (IsShown fallback, as OptionsCombat.lua:66-71); register UPDATE_BINDINGS when any is, unregister when none. Called on row build, on release, from the ctx.panel OnShow/OnHide hooks LK-12 installs (extend them), and at the start of each dispatch.
- `lib.__OnKeybindEvent(event)`: sync first; nothing on screen -> return having drawn nothing; else schedule ONE repaint: if `lib.__keybindRepaintPending` return; else set it and `C_Timer.After(0, flush)` (no C_Timer: flush now). flush clears the flag and repaints every live on-screen row (slots + set line) from GetBindingKey. A listening slot keeps S.LISTENING through a repaint.
- OnShow re-read: the ctx.panel OnShow hook repaints that ctx's rows (QuickComms precedent db8f7a6:settings/Dials.lua:409-412). Repaints only read, so they are allowed in combat.
- Every function CCN <= 15.

